{"id": "unknown-2026-08-17-004", "date": "2026-08-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 34, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh seeks support from Australia for joining RCEP", "content": "Bangladesh has sought Australia’s support for joining the RCEP grouping to enjoy preferential market access after its graduation from the LDC status. \nBangladesh Commerce secretary Mohammad Ataur Rahman Khan proposed in Canberra that Australia consider concluding a bilateral FTA. \nAustralian officials said they would consult with stakeholders and determine the appropriate course of action. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-seeks-support-from-australia-for-joining-rcep-312680-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
